:"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.northtyneside.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-23","committee":"Cabinet","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.northtyneside.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-26","committee":"Council","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.northtyneside.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-07-27","committee":"Cabinet","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.northtyneside.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-08-12","committee":"Audit Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.northtyneside.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-09","committee":"Overview & Scrutiny Co-ordination & Finance Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.northtyneside.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-21","committee":"Cabinet","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.northtyneside.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-24","committee":"Council","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.northtyneside.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"External quality assessment of internal audit function is eight years overdue and scheduled only for consideration in 2026/27","lead":"External validation of internal audit quality is required assurance; without it there is no independent assessment whether the audit function itself is operating effectively","iso":"2026-08-12","paper_title":"Agenda Item 9 - Internal Audit Annual Report and Opinion 2025-26","paper_url":"https://northtyneside.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s37527/37527.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Internal audit activity was resourced below the agreed plan for 2025/26","lead":"Reduced audit capacity means less independent oversight of financial controls; this narrows the probability of detecting control failures or financial irregularities","iso":"2026-08-12","paper_title":"Agenda Item 9 - Internal Audit Annual Report and Opinion 2025-26","paper_url":"https://northtyneside.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s37527/37527.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Home care payment system control weaknesses as delegation and review processes embed on new platform","lead":"Adult social care typically represents a significant proportion of council spend; incomplete controls on a new financial system present material implementation risk until fully embedded","iso":"2026-08-12","paper_title":"Agenda Item 9 - Internal Audit Annual Report and Opinion 2025-26","paper_url":"https://northtyneside.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s37527/37527.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-08-12","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Agenda Item 9 - Internal Audit Annual Report and Opinion 2025-26","paper_url":"https://northtyneside.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s37527/37527.pdf","headline":"External quality assessment of internal audit function is eight years overdue and scheduled only for consideration in 2026/27","detail":"Standards require external assessment every five years. North Tyneside's last external assessment was February 2018. The council acknowledges non-conformance but assesses the risk as low given annual self-assessment.","category":"governance","matters":"External validation of internal audit quality is required assurance; without it there is no independent assessment whether the audit function itself is operating effectively","figures":"Last external assessment: February 2018; standard requirement: every five years","quote":"This is required every five years, but North Tyneside's Internal Audit service was last subject to external assessment in February 2018.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-08-12","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Agenda Item 9 - Internal Audit Annual Report and Opinion 2025-26","paper_url":"https://northtyneside.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s37527/37527.pdf","headline":"Internal audit activity was resourced below the agreed plan for 2025/26","detail":"The council had fewer internal audit resources available during the year than established when the annual plan was agreed in May 2025. This directly reduced audit coverage compared to what was intended.","category":"governance","matters":"Reduced audit capacity means less independent oversight of financial controls; this narrows the probability of detecting control failures or financial irregularities","figures":"Resource levels reduced mid-year; shortfall magnitude not quantified","quote":"The overall level of resources available for internal audit activity during 2025/26 was less than that established when agreeing the annual plan in May 2025.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-08-12","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Agenda Item 9 - Internal Audit Annual Report and Opinion 2025-26","paper_url":"https://northtyneside.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s37527/37527.pdf","headline":"Home care payment system control weaknesses as delegation and review processes embed on new platform","detail":"The adult social care payment system received limited assurance due to incomplete implementation of delegation schemes and review procedures. The audit explicitly notes the system is 'still relatively new and arrangements are evolving,' indicating controls remain in development phase.","category":"audit","matters":"Adult social care typically represents a significant proportion of council spend; incomplete controls on a new financial system present material implementation risk until fully embedded","figures":"One of seven limited assurance opinions issued in 2025/26","quote":"Home Care Payment Arrangements \u2013 the matters relate to implementing a local scheme of delegation within the software used to manage payments and review of activity managed through this system. The system is still relatively new and arrangements are evolving.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-08-12","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Agenda Item 9 - Internal Audit Annual Report and Opinion 2025-26","paper_url":"https://northtyneside.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s37527/37527.pdf","headline":"Supplier database maintenance has limited assurance due to incomplete system implementation and underdeveloped fraud controls","detail":"The creditors audit found that the new system is not fully utilising its functionality and anti-fraud arrangements are not adequately developed. This represents a control gap in a core financial function at a time when the council faces acknowledged financial pressures.","category":"audit","matters":"Creditor controls are fundamental to preventing fraud and ensuring accurate financial reporting; weaknesses here create risk of undetected errors or fraudulent payments","figures":"One of seven limited assurance opinions issued in 2025/26","quote":"Creditors (suppliers database maintenance) \u2013 the matters relate to the implementation of the new system, not utilising all functionality and need to develop anti-fraud arrangements which are specific to this area","material":true},{"iso":"2026-08-12","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Agenda Item 7 - Appendix A - Draft Annual Governance Statement 202526","paper_url":"https://northtyneside.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s37525/37525.pdf","headline":"Council must develop action plan to address strategic recommendations from Independent Financial Resilience Review during 2026/27","detail":"The AGS action plan explicitly requires development of an action plan to meet recommendations from the Financial Resilience Review, to be incorporated into performance and finance reports to Cabinet. Target completion is during 2026/27.","category":"governance","matters":"Active remediation of external financial pressure recommendations is required; absence of a completed plan indicates the resilience issues remain unresolved.","figures":"2026/27 financial year","quote":"Develop an Action Plan to meet the Strategic Recommendations set out in the Independent Financial Resilience Review Report and for that Plan to be incorporated into the Performance and Finance reports presented to Cabinet","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-08-12"},"name":"North Tyneside","findings_total":49,"news_drafts_total":3}}